course: dictionary
lesson: 11595
title: Strong words for bad things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you that something is not just bad, but very bad. «Appalling» is one of them. The clues around it show you how strong it is. «The rubbish left in the park was appalling: broken bottles and old tyres lay everywhere.» Broken bottles and old tyres are nasty and unsafe, so appalling must mean very shocking and unpleasant.
explain: In everyday speech, people also use appalling to mean very bad, like «appalling weather». «The weather on our camping trip was appalling: rain all day and wind that blew the tents over.» Nobody enjoys weather like that, so appalling is a strong way to say it was very bad.
explain: Ask yourself what would fit in the same place. In «appalling handwriting», you could swap in very bad handwriting and the sentence still makes sense. Then ask whether the word feels stronger than the word you would normally use. If it does, the author chose it for a reason.
fact: «Appalling» means very shocking and unpleasant.
fact: In informal speech, «appalling» means very bad, as in «appalling weather» or «appalling handwriting».
fact: «Appalling» is stronger than «bad»: it shows the author feels strongly about the thing.
fact: Phrases like «appalling conditions» and «appalling behaviour» show that something is wrong and should not be happening.
fact: A good check is to swap in «very bad» or «very shocking» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The rubbish left in the park was appalling: broken bottles and old tyres lay everywhere.» What does appalling mean here? | Tiny and light | *Very shocking and unpleasant | Very quiet and calm | Lovely and clean
exercise: Dad says, «The weather on our camping trip was appalling.» What does appalling mean? | *Very bad | Warm and sunny | Windy in a fun way | Foggy only at night
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to appalling in «appalling behaviour»? | *shocking | gentle | sleepy | bright
test: «The children's handwriting was appalling, so the teacher could not read a single word.» What does appalling mean here? | *Very bad, so nobody could read it | Neat and tidy | Very bad | Colourful and large
test: Why might an author choose appalling instead of bad? | *It is stronger and shows the thing is very shocking or very bad | It means exactly the same as bad, so there is no reason to pick it | It means happy | It is a shorter word
exam: In «The appalling conditions in the old barn made the animals ill.», which clue shows that appalling means very bad? | *The animals became ill | The word conditions is long | The sentence has a full stop | The barn was red
